{{Quote|The continued and inexplicable Ghorman resistance to Imperial norms. Terrorism strikes again in Ghorman. Just three weeks after events in Corei and Jel-Novi, there was a firebombing last night at the Naval Terminal in Palmo. You can see, behind me, vapor and thermal smoke still rising from the site&hellip;|A reporter|audio=AfterEventsInCoreiAndJelNovi-Messenger.flac|<ref name="Messenger" />}}
'''Corei''' was a location on<ref name="Messenger" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="OYL">{{Andor|One Year Later}}</ref> [[Ghorman]]. In [[2 BBY]], an [[Event in Corei|event]] occurred in Corei that the [[Galactic Empire]] characterized as [[Terrorist|terrorism]]<ref name="Messenger" /> as part of its [[anti-Ghorman whispering campaign]], aiming to reinforce control of Ghorman so as to [[Mining|mine]] the planet's [[kalkite]], a [[mineral]] needed to coat the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star's]] [[Hypermatter reactor|hypermatter annihilation reactor lens]].<ref name="OYL" /> Three [[standard week|weeks]] after the event in Corei, following a [[Firebombing at the Imperial Naval Terminal|firebombing]] at the [[Imperial Naval Terminal]] in Ghorman's [[capital]] [[city]] [[Palmo]], a [[Unidentified reporter 1|reporter]] mentioned the event in Corei as an example of terrorism during a [[Propaganda|pro-Imperial news report]].<ref name="Messenger" />

==Behind the scenes==
Corei was mentioned in "[[Messenger (episode)|Messenger]],"<ref name="Messenger" /> the seventh episode in the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', which aired on [[May 6]], [[2025]].<ref name="Companion">{{InsiderCite|233|Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion}}</ref>

